index 0000000..2eafad6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/CAPACITY.md
@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+# Aggregate content capacity
+
+`Memory({ maxContentBytes })` optionally configures the aggregate content budget. Omission preserves the existing `limits.maxBytes` default. Only a positive safe integer is accepted. The effective budget is enforced before continuing a partial manifest and on unchanged complete manifests as well as each new batch. Explicitly configured budgets are recorded on subsequent manifests.
+
+This budget does not change file eligibility, per-file size, ordering, Git revision or the immutable saved source plan. Changing it therefore resumes the existing cursor and blob cache; it does not rewrite the plan, delete state or reread completed blobs. The original `limits` object and identity remain unchanged. Changing filtering limits still rejects the plan. Budget changes are operator configuration and never derived from repository content.
+
+This isolated vendored repository imports exactly the 38 code files from approved reader archive c55edff7ab8b991fee2ce4a1a5fd6bd20d16ec113e50834d94322e5cb1f0df13 (original reader revision 9c477cebfff7383d1b8c2b7064fcc5462a02f039). Its Git baseline is a new import commit, not a claim of original Git ancestry. Runtime manifests include only the original 38 code paths; tests and this document are not loaded in production.
